00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.880
might have better systems than the ones that we&nbsp;
do. They don't necessarily have perfect systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.920
And you have to imagine a triangle with three, you&nbsp;
know, like it's a triangle. It has three points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:03:00.800
where there are these three elements, you've&nbsp;
got cost, quality and access, and every system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:09.360
is trying to make a dot somewhere between those&nbsp;
three. If you go lower cost and higher access,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:17.120
that puts downward pressure on quality, all else&nbsp;
being equal. If you have higher cost and higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:23.920
quality, then you're pulling away from everybody&nbsp;
having access and every system is basically trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.680
to find a point on that triangle. And the&nbsp;
French system is not perfect. I talked about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.600
