the system in Singapore. There's no perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:40.240
system. The point is, do we want to prioritize&nbsp;
quality? And in quality I include the time you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.720
have to wait until you get treatment. Do&nbsp;
we want to prioritize quality and or cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:53.920
and or access? And many countries do better than&nbsp;
us on any of those three or even two of those.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.600
And then when you say, Well, which countries do&nbsp;
better on all three, then it becomes a question of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:04.160
for what part of the population. And I don't&nbsp;
know that, you know, I don't know enough about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:09.680
